---@field state? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceStateEnum Output only. The current state of this instance.
---@field customerManagedKey? string Optional. The KMS key reference that the customer provides when trying to create the instance.
---@field host? string Output only. Hostname or IP address of the exposed Redis endpoint used by clients to connect to the service.
---@field persistenceIamIdentity? string Output only. Cloud IAM identity used by import / export operations to transfer data to/from Cloud Storage. Format is "serviceAccount:". The value may change over time for a given instance so should be checked before each import/export operation.
---@field statusMessage? string Output only. Additional information about the current status of this instance, if available.
---@field redisConfigs? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Redis configuration parameters, according to [Redis configuration](https://redis.io/docs/latest/operate/oss_and_stack/management/config/). Currently, the only supported parameters are: Redis version 3.2 and newer: * maxmemory-policy * notify-keyspace-events Redis version 4.0 and newer: * activedefrag * lfu-decay-time * lfu-log-factor * maxmemory-gb Redis version 5.0 and newer: * stream-node-max-bytes * stream-node-max-entries
---@field persistenceConfig? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PersistenceConfig Optional. Persistence configuration parameters
---@field suspensionReasons? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceSuspensionReasonsItemEnumList Optional. reasons that causes instance in "SUSPENDED" state.
---@field maintenanceVersion? string Optional. The self service update maintenance version. The version is date based such as "20210712_00_00".
---@field maintenancePolicy? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.MaintenancePolicy Optional. The maintenance policy for the instance. If not provided, maintenance events can be performed at any time.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Optional. Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field reservedIpRange? string Optional. For DIRECT_PEERING mode, the CIDR range of internal addresses that are reserved for this instance. Range must be unique and non-overlapping with existing subnets in an authorized network. For PRIVATE_SERVICE_ACCESS mode, the name of one allocated IP address ranges associated with this private service access connection. If not provided, the service will choose an unused /29 block, for example, 10.0.0.0/29 or 192.168.0.0/29. For READ_REPLICAS_ENABLED the default block size is /28.
---@field name? string Required. Unique name of the resource in this scope including project and location using the form: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location_id}/instances/{instance_id}` Note: Redis instances are managed and addressed at regional level so location_id here refers to a GCP region; however, users may choose which specific zone (or collection of zones for cross-zone instances) an instance should be provisioned in. Refer to location_id and alternative_location_id fields for more details.
---@field alternativeLocationId? string Optional. If specified, at least one node will be provisioned in this zone in addition to the zone specified in location_id. Only applicable to standard tier. If provided, it must be a different zone from the one provided in [location_id]. Additional nodes beyond the first 2 will be placed in zones selected by the service.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Resource labels to represent user provided metadata
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Optional. Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field readReplicasMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceReadReplicasModeEnum Optional. Read replicas mode for the instance. Defaults to READ_REPLICAS_DISABLED.
---@field locationId? string Optional. The zone where the instance will be provisioned. If not provided, the service will choose a zone from the specified region for the instance. For standard tier, additional nodes will be added across multiple zones for protection against zonal failures. If specified, at least one node will be provisioned in this zone.
---@field secondaryIpRange? string Optional. Additional IP range for node placement. Required when enabling read replicas on an existing instance. For DIRECT_PEERING mode value must be a CIDR range of size /28, or "auto". For PRIVATE_SERVICE_ACCESS mode value must be the name of an allocated address range associated with the private service access connection, or "auto".
---@field authorizedNetwork? string Optional. The full name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/vpc) to which the instance is connected. If left unspecified, the `default` network will be used.
---@field port? number Output only. The port number of the exposed Redis endpoint.
---@field tags? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Immutable. Tag keys/values directly bound to this resource. For example: "123/environment": "production", "123/costCenter": "marketing"
---@field readEndpointPort? number Output only. The port number of the exposed readonly redis endpoint. Standard tier only. Write requests should target 'port'.
---@field serverCaCerts? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.TlsCertificateList Output only. List of server CA certificates for the instance.
---@field currentLocationId? string Output only. The current zone where the Redis primary node is located. In basic tier, this will always be the same as [location_id]. In standard tier, this can be the zone of any node in the instance.
---@field maintenanceSchedule? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.MaintenanceSchedule Output only. Date and time of upcoming maintenance events which have been scheduled.
---@field transitEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceTransitEncryptionModeEnum Optional. The TLS mode of the Redis instance. If not provided, TLS is disabled for the instance.

