---@field automatedBackupConfig? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.AutomatedBackupConfig Optional. The automated backup config for the cluster.
---@field clusterEndpoints? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ClusterEndpointList Optional. A list of cluster endpoints.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Labels to represent user-provided metadata.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ClusterStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of this cluster. Can be CREATING, READY, UPDATING, DELETING and SUSPENDED
---@field zoneDistributionConfig? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ZoneDistributionConfig Optional. This config will be used to determine how the customer wants us to distribute cluster resources within the region.
---@field replicaCount? number Optional. The number of replica nodes per shard.
---@field preciseSizeGb? number Output only. Precise value of redis memory size in GB for the entire cluster.
---@field rotateServerCertificate? boolean Optional. Input only. Rotate the server certificates.
---@field gcsSource? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.GcsBackupSource Optional. Backups stored in Cloud Storage buckets. The Cloud Storage buckets need to be the same region as the clusters. Read permission is required to import from the provided Cloud Storage objects.
---@field uid? string Output only. System assigned, unique identifier for the cluster.
---@field discoveryEndpoints? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.DiscoveryEndpointList Output only. Endpoints created on each given network, for Redis clients to connect to the cluster. Currently only one discovery endpoint is supported.
---@field asyncClusterEndpointsDeletionEnabled? boolean Optional. If true, cluster endpoints that are created and registered by customers can be deleted asynchronously. That is, such a cluster endpoint can be de-registered before the forwarding rules in the cluster endpoint are deleted.
---@field crossClusterReplicationConfig? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.CrossClusterReplicationConfig Optional. Cross cluster replication config.
---@field managedBackupSource? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ManagedBackupSource Optional. Backups generated and managed by memorystore service.
---@field ondemandMaintenance? boolean Optional. Input only. Ondemand maintenance for the cluster. This field can be used to trigger ondemand critical update on the cluster.
---@field maintenanceVersion? string Optional. This field can be used to trigger self service update to indicate the desired maintenance version. The input to this field can be determined by the available_maintenance_versions field.
---@field encryptionInfo? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.EncryptionInfo Output only. Encryption information of the data at rest of the cluster.
---@field aclPolicyInfo? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.AclPolicyInfo Output only. Details of the applied ACL policy.
---@field aclPolicy? string Optional. The ACL policy to be applied to the cluster.
---@field allowFewerZonesDeployment? boolean Optional. Immutable. Deprecated, do not use.
---@field simulateMaintenanceEvent? boolean Optional. Input only. Simulate a maintenance event.
---@field kmsKey? string Optional. The KMS key used to encrypt the at-rest data of the cluster.
---@field stateInfo? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StateInfo Output only. Additional information about the current state of the cluster.
---@field nodeType? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ClusterNodeTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of a redis node in the cluster. NodeType determines the underlying machine-type of a redis node.
---@field maintenancePolicy? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ClusterMaintenancePolicy Optional. ClusterMaintenancePolicy determines when to allow or deny updates.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Optional. Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field sizeGb? number Output only. Redis memory size in GB for the entire cluster rounded up to the next integer.
---@field pscServiceAttachments? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PscServiceAttachmentList Output only. Service attachment details to configure Psc connections
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Optional. Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field pscConfigs? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PscConfigList Optional. Each PscConfig configures the consumer network where IPs will be designated to the cluster for client access through Private Service Connect Automation. Currently, only one PscConfig is supported.
---@field transitEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.ClusterTransitEncryptionModeEnum|string Optional. The in-transit encryption for the Redis cluster. If not provided, encryption is disabled for the cluster.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp associated with the cluster creation request.
---@field requestId? string Optional. Idempotent request UUID.
---@field name string Required. Identifier. Unique name of the resource in this scope including project and location using the form: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location_id}/clusters/{cluster_id}`
---@field updateMask? string Required. Mask of fields to update. At least one path must be supplied in this field. The elements of the repeated paths field may only include these fields from Cluster: * `size_gb` * `replica_count` * `cluster_endpoints`

---@class gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PatchProjectsLocationsInstancesRequest
---@field displayName? string An arbitrary and optional user-provided name for the instance.
---@field nodes? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.NodeInfoList Output only. Info per node.
---@field readEndpoint? string Output only. Hostname or IP address of the exposed readonly Redis endpoint. Standard tier only. Targets all healthy replica nodes in instance. Replication is asynchronous and replica nodes will exhibit some lag behind the primary. Write requests must target 'host'.
---@field availableMaintenanceVersions? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringList Optional. The available maintenance versions that an instance could update to.
---@field memorySizeGb? number Required. Redis memory size in GiB.
---@field authEnabled? boolean Optional. Indicates whether OSS Redis AUTH is enabled for the instance. If set to "true" AUTH is enabled on the instance. Default value is "false" meaning AUTH is disabled.
---@field connectMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceConnectModeEnum|string Optional. The network connect mode of the Redis instance. If not provided, the connect mode defaults to DIRECT_PEERING.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the instance was created.
---@field replicaCount? number Optional. The number of replica nodes. The valid range for the Standard Tier with read replicas enabled is [1-5] and defaults to 2. If read replicas are not enabled for a Standard Tier instance, the only valid value is 1 and the default is 1. The valid value for basic tier is 0 and the default is also 0.
---@field tier? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceTierEnum|string Required. The service tier of the instance.
---@field redisVersion? string Optional. The version of Redis software. If not provided, latest supported version will be used. Currently, the supported values are: * `REDIS_3_2` for Redis 3.2 compatibility * `REDIS_4_0` for Redis 4.0 compatibility (default) * `REDIS_5_0` for Redis 5.0 compatibility * `REDIS_6_X` for Redis 6.x compatibility * `REDIS_7_0` for Redis 7.0 compatibility
---@field state? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of this instance.
---@field customerManagedKey? string Optional. The KMS key reference that the customer provides when trying to create the instance.
---@field host? string Output only. Hostname or IP address of the exposed Redis endpoint used by clients to connect to the service.
---@field persistenceIamIdentity? string Output only. Cloud IAM identity used by import / export operations to transfer data to/from Cloud Storage. Format is "serviceAccount:". The value may change over time for a given instance so should be checked before each import/export operation.
---@field statusMessage? string Output only. Additional information about the current status of this instance, if available.
---@field redisConfigs? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Redis configuration parameters, according to [Redis configuration](https://redis.io/docs/latest/operate/oss_and_stack/management/config/). Currently, the only supported parameters are: Redis version 3.2 and newer: * maxmemory-policy * notify-keyspace-events Redis version 4.0 and newer: * activedefrag * lfu-decay-time * lfu-log-factor * maxmemory-gb Redis version 5.0 and newer: * stream-node-max-bytes * stream-node-max-entries
---@field persistenceConfig? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PersistenceConfig Optional. Persistence configuration parameters
---@field suspensionReasons? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceSuspensionReasonsItemEnumList Optional. reasons that causes instance in "SUSPENDED" state.
---@field maintenanceVersion? string Optional. The self service update maintenance version. The version is date based such as "20210712_00_00".
---@field maintenancePolicy? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.MaintenancePolicy Optional. The maintenance policy for the instance. If not provided, maintenance events can be performed at any time.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Optional. Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field reservedIpRange? string Optional. For DIRECT_PEERING mode, the CIDR range of internal addresses that are reserved for this instance. Range must be unique and non-overlapping with existing subnets in an authorized network. For PRIVATE_SERVICE_ACCESS mode, the name of one allocated IP address ranges associated with this private service access connection. If not provided, the service will choose an unused /29 block, for example, 10.0.0.0/29 or 192.168.0.0/29. For READ_REPLICAS_ENABLED the default block size is /28.
---@field alternativeLocationId? string Optional. If specified, at least one node will be provisioned in this zone in addition to the zone specified in location_id. Only applicable to standard tier. If provided, it must be a different zone from the one provided in [location_id]. Additional nodes beyond the first 2 will be placed in zones selected by the service.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Resource labels to represent user provided metadata
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Optional. Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field readReplicasMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceReadReplicasModeEnum|string Optional. Read replicas mode for the instance. Defaults to READ_REPLICAS_DISABLED.
---@field locationId? string Optional. The zone where the instance will be provisioned. If not provided, the service will choose a zone from the specified region for the instance. For standard tier, additional nodes will be added across multiple zones for protection against zonal failures. If specified, at least one node will be provisioned in this zone.
---@field secondaryIpRange? string Optional. Additional IP range for node placement. Required when enabling read replicas on an existing instance. For DIRECT_PEERING mode value must be a CIDR range of size /28, or "auto". For PRIVATE_SERVICE_ACCESS mode value must be the name of an allocated address range associated with the private service access connection, or "auto".
---@field authorizedNetwork? string Optional. The full name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/vpc) to which the instance is connected. If left unspecified, the `default` network will be used.
---@field port? number Output only. The port number of the exposed Redis endpoint.
---@field tags? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Immutable. Tag keys/values directly bound to this resource. For example: "123/environment": "production", "123/costCenter": "marketing"
---@field readEndpointPort? number Output only. The port number of the exposed readonly redis endpoint. Standard tier only. Write requests should target 'port'.
---@field serverCaCerts? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.TlsCertificateList Output only. List of server CA certificates for the instance.
---@field currentLocationId? string Output only. The current zone where the Redis primary node is located. In basic tier, this will always be the same as [location_id]. In standard tier, this can be the zone of any node in the instance.
---@field maintenanceSchedule? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.MaintenanceSchedule Output only. Date and time of upcoming maintenance events which have been scheduled.
---@field transitEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.InstanceTransitEncryptionModeEnum|string Optional. The TLS mode of the Redis instance. If not provided, TLS is disabled for the instance.
---@field updateMask? string Required. Mask of fields to update. At least one path must be supplied in this field. The elements of the repeated paths field may only include these fields from Instance: * `displayName` * `labels` * `memorySizeGb` * `redisConfig` * `replica_count`
---@field name string Required. Unique name of the resource in this scope including project and location using the form: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location_id}/instances/{instance_id}` Note: Redis instances are managed and addressed at regional level so location_id here refers to a GCP region; however, users may choose which specific zone (or collection of zones for cross-zone instances) an instance should be provisioned in. Refer to location_id and alternative_location_id fields for more details.

---Configuration of the persistence functionality.
---@class gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PersistenceConfig
---@field rdbSnapshotPeriod? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PersistenceConfigRdbSnapshotPeriodEnum|string Optional. Period between RDB snapshots. Snapshots will be attempted every period starting from the provided snapshot start time. For example, a start time of 01/01/2033 06:45 and SIX_HOURS snapshot period will do nothing until 01/01/2033, and then trigger snapshots every day at 06:45, 12:45, 18:45, and 00:45 the next day, and so on. If not provided, TWENTY_FOUR_HOURS will be used as default.
---@field rdbSnapshotStartTime? string Optional. Date and time that the first snapshot was/will be attempted, and to which future snapshots will be aligned. If not provided, the current time will be used.
---@field persistenceMode? gcp.unstable.redis_v1beta1.PersistenceConfigPersistenceModeEnum|string Optional. Controls whether Persistence features are enabled. If not provided, the existing value will be used.
---@field rdbNextSnapshotTime? string Output only. The next time that a snapshot attempt is scheduled to occur.

